{
 "designs": {
  "d24": [
   {
    "text": "Read the drop. Predators turn bacterial nitrogen into ammonium.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/d24-1.jpg"
   }
  ],
  "p18": [
   {
    "text": "Vampire amoeba.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p18-1.jpg"
   }
  ],
  "d20": [
   {
    "text": "Julia's worm bin. Vermicompost, made at home.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/d20-1.jpg"
   }
  ],
  "p12": [
   {
    "text": "Before you bag those leaves, read this.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p12-1.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "Leaf litter is rich in carbon and lignin.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p12-2.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "Fungi are the main decomposers of lignin.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p12-3.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "That feeds the fungal soils trees and shrubs prefer.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p12-4.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "A layer of leaves shields the soil over winter.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p12-5.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "On a lawn, shred the leaves and move them onto your beds.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p12-6.jpg"
   }
  ],
  "p24": [
   {
    "text": "440,000,000,000,000,000,000 soil nematodes on Earth, by the 2019 estimate in Nature.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p24-1.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "57 billion for every person alive.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p24-2.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "Most feed on bacteria and fungi, and release nitrogen right at the root.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p24-3.jpg"
   }
  ],
  "p02": [
   {
    "text": "Meet our mentors Casey Williams",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p02-1.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "A bacterial-feeding nematode, 40x, photographed by Casey. “I am deeply grateful that I get to learn from my students as well as teach them.”",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p02-2.jpg"
   },
   {
    "text": "Thank you, Casey.",
    "image": "/wormhole/tiles/p02-3.jpg"
   }
  ]
 },
